# agents/permissions.retire — rules `dots` REMOVES from every agent's config: the other
# half of add-and-retire. A rule dropped from permissions.allow lives on wherever it
# already landed, so taking one back means moving it here. Same syntax as .allow; a
# rule in BOTH lists is an error — `t permissions` refuses to apply anything until one
# side wins. A retired rule is removed from ~/.claude/settings.json and cursor's
# cli-config.json (every occurrence) and simply stops being generated for codex.

# subsumed by Bash(launchctl:*) in permissions.allow (2026-09-14)
Bash(launchctl kickstart:*)
